{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/packet-v9-2.md'","aggregated_output":"# Packet v9-2\n\n**The question:** Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform begin shipping by January 31, 2027?\n\nDue 2027-01-31. Possible answers:\n- 1 Yes: NVIDIA begins shipping the Vera Rubin platform on or before January 31, 2027.\n- 2 No: NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Vera Rubin platform by January 31, 2027.\n\n**6 statements read on 2026-09-24:**\n\n- **v9-2-1** (stored attribution: Aolani): Aolani said on September 21 that it plans to deploy 22,000 Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs across two AI factories in Malaysia and the Philippines in early 2027; the expansion would bring its total GPU deployment above 48,000 and AI factory capacity above 100 MW.\n  - Passage: \"Singapore-founded AI cloud provider Aolani said Sept. 21 that it plans to deploy 22,000 Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs across two AI factories in Malaysia and the Philippines in early 2027. The expansion would take Aolani’s total GPU deployment above 48,000 and its AI factory capacity past 100 MW.\"\n- **v9-2-2** (stored attribution: NVIDIA management): NVIDIA management guided to about 70% total revenue growth in FY2028, its first full-year-ahead revenue growth guidance.\n  - Passage: \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead.\"\n- **v9-2-3** (stored attribution: Zacks.com): The Zacks consensus estimates imply NVIDIA earnings growth of approximately 93.9% in FY2027 and 65.8% in FY2028.\n  - Passage: \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and 2028 earnings implies a year-over-year increase of approximately 93.9% and 65.8%, respectively.\"\n- **v9-2-4** (stored attribution: Intel management): Intel management said purpose-built silicon revenue was approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate and targeted $4 billion in the near future.\n  - Passage: \"During the last earnings call, management noted that purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, and the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\"\n- **v9-2-5** (stored attribution: Trefis, the article’s author): The 33 analyst estimates cited by Trefis for NVIDIA FY2028 earnings ranged from $12.62 to $17.49 per share.\n  - Passage: \"The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n- **v9-2-6** (stored attribution: The Gears of War: E-Day developer): RTX Mega Geometry 2.0 is planned for Gears of War: E-Day; the article gives no release date.\n  - Passage: \"The other big addition to the RTX Kit is RTX Mega Geometry 2.0, coming soon to Gears of War: E-Day, so stay tuned for our coverage.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":\"v9-2-1\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The deployment concerns Blackwell Ultra GPUs, not the Vera Rubin platform.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v9-2-2\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Overall revenue growth guidance does not establish when Vera Rubin will begin shipping.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v9-2-3\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"NVIDIA earnings growth estimates do not establish the platform's shipping date.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v9-2-4\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Intel's silicon revenue targets do not address Vera Rubin shipping.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v9-2-5\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"NVIDIA earnings estimates do not establish the platform's shipping date.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v9-2-6\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The planned game graphics feature does not address Vera Rubin shipping.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"items\":6}"}}
